# DDRMAX - Dance Dance Revolution 6th Mix (G*B19 VER. JAA), Konami 2001: a game, from what ddrmax-install left (its NVRAM). Power-on: the
# flash and PC Card checksums, then NOTE 605 (RTC-RAM cleared): Test at 1500. Boot checks, loading,
# attract. Two coins at frame 9000, then Start every 300 frames through the style, character or
# difficulty, and music selects (their defaults); the first stage, with its MP3 music, played by
# stepping on all four panels every 8 frames from frame 11000: some arrows are hit, some missed.
# Its result by frame ~16200, then the second stage's music select. Hashes the main RAM every
# frame and snapshots every 60 frames, to compare HIRAKU's 573 core with MAME through a song.
game ddrmax

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 1500 press "Service Mode" 8   # NOTE 605
at 9000 press "Coin 1" 8
at 9040 press "Coin 1" 8
at 9300 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 9600 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 9900 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 10200 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 10500 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 10800 press "1 Player Start" 8
from 11000 every 8 press "P1 Left" 4
from 11000 every 8 press "P1 Down" 4
from 11000 every 8 press "P1 Up" 4
from 11000 every 8 press "P1 Right" 4
from 0 every 60 snap
at 18000 quit
